<http://data.silknow.org/object/43c11465-f713-3ec3-b329-63bc0660f6db>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "The design is a debased form of Group 1 sub-group 2 as defined by Jennifer Wearden in 'Azerbaijanian Embroideries: A Synthesis of Contrasts' in Hali Issue 59, October 1991 pp. 102-111 characterized by a central medallion but by cartouches; these are usually worked in cross stitch so technically this cover belongs to the surface darning group of the early to mid-18th century"@en ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/88edf954-2512-31f6-9ead-eb94e7d2b4e1> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/information/bibliography> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The design is a debased form of Group 1 sub-group 2 as defined by Jennifer Wearden in 'Azerbaijanian Embroideries: A Synthesis of Contrasts' in Hali Issue 59, October 1991 pp. 102-111 characterized by a central medallion but by cartouches; these are usually worked in cross stitch so technically this cover belongs to the surface darning group of the early to mid-18th century"@en .

